      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — See inline comments. [[trajectory](https://goto.corp.google.com/traj/c4516b3c-c44b-42d1-afd5-83ae3f3a11e0)]\n\n### Review Summary\n\n*   **Functionality:** ❌ **Changes Requested.** `cros_flash_rtkfp_get_protect` incorrectly returns `0` (writable) when `sw_protected` is false due to an early return condition. This masks the true hardware state and creates an inconsistency because `write` will still reject the operation if the hardware BP bits are set. This bypass also causes `test_protect_at_boot_only_without_sw_lock` to fail. See inline comment for the fix.\n*   **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ✅ The driver properly abstracts the status register parsing and translates it into standard `EC_FLASH_PROTECT_*` flags using the shared `spi_flash_reg_to_protect` utility, avoiding redundant parsing logic.\n*   **Code Simplicity:** ✅ The `#ifdef` blocks and `else if` chains in `cros_flash_rtkfp_get_protect_flags` were successfully flattened and unified, making the logic much more declarative.\n*   **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ✅ The use of `\u003cstdbool.h\u003e` and `bool` for `sw_protected` is correct, and the control flow uses declarative checks.\n*   **Security:** ✅ Status register parsing explicitly rejects inconsistent SRP bit settings or undecodable configurations by failing closed with `EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ERROR_INCONSISTENT` and `EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ERROR_UNKNOWN`.\n*   **Testing:** ✅ Comprehensive coverage is provided for the protection query API, including exact hardware boundary checks (`WP_BANK - 1`, `WP_BANK`), hardware initialization dependencies, and error handling paths.\n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** ✅ `Size: M (+197, -3)`. The CL successfully complies with the Single Logical Change rule by isolating the state queries into this CL and moving the mutation operations to a separate CL.\n*   **Commit Message:** ✅ The message is concise, avoids diff narration, focuses on the core intent of mapping BP bits/software locks to the `cros_flash` API flags, and includes the proper issue and test verification tags.\n[🔗](http://go/tj/c4516b3c-c44b-42d1-afd5-83ae3f3a11e0)",
