      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested**\n\nThe early return here creates a state inconsistency and will cause your new `test_protect_at_boot_only_without_sw_lock` test to fail. \n\nWhen `!data-\u003esw_protected` is true (e.g. WP is deasserted) and `CONFIG_WP_STORAGE_OFF \u003d\u003d 0`, `addr_start \u003e\u003d 0` is always true. This causes `get_protect` to blindly return `0` (writable) for all banks, bypassing `flash_check_prot_reg`. \n\nHowever, `cros_flash_rtkfp_write` unconditionally checks `flash_check_prot_reg` and will still return `EC_ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED` if the hardware BP bits are set. If the hardware rejects the write, `get_protect` must accurately report the bank as protected (`1`). \n\nRemoving this bypass aligns `get_protect` with `write` and fixes the failing `zassert_equal(cros_flash_physical_get_protect(cros_flash_dev, 0), 1)` in your test suite:\n\n```c\n\t/*\n\t * The physical_get_protect returns protection state until reboot,\n\t * so it is used to determine *_NOW flags.\n\t */\n\tif (flash_check_prot_reg(dev, addr_start, CONFIG_FLASH_BANK_SIZE) \u003d\u003d\n\t    EC_ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED) {\n\t\treturn 1;\n\t}\n\n\treturn 0;\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/c4516b3c-c44b-42d1-afd5-83ae3f3a11e0)",
